t}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=5{x}_{2}-{t}^{2}{x}_{1}+t{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=-{t}^{2}{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}+t{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can represent this system as the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -{t}^{2} & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ t{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367589 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a7f2a0b-777f-5d63-9f3a-3b3f4a6969d8" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Inhomogeneous ODE as a Matrix Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6f11e82-391f-5219-a855-ab975d662aee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367591} {:answer/id #uuid "8899737f-1a2b-54dd-901b-e10b80abcd56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8899737f-1a2b-54dd-901b-e10b80abcd56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367592} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b090c15-2670-5178-b98f-5259d8d6959e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367590} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dca06435-52cb-5706-bb15-bc32d9ae0057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dca06435-52cb-5706-bb15-bc32d9ae0057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 1